# zbc: a full-index-coverage certificate for `for` loops, so a fixed array a
#      loop provably fills in full is not reported as still `undefined`.
# AUTHORED, not captured; 0001-0004 are byte-for-byte untouched.
# Base: upstream 419d153ca411d1698899992d86c51eb9a7e14919 + 0001-0004.
# Apply with: git -C <checkout> apply --whitespace=nowarn -p1 <this file>, AFTER 0001, 0002, 0003, 0004.
# source_digest: b794e308…e5e3d2 -> ddcb7de4c311651caba3133fa3e15915bc4bf4df3815da36bc0442962c56c868
#
# THE DEFECT. lowerFor gives every loop an unconditional header->exit edge, so a local read
# after the loop is reachable on a path where the body never ran. For `var arr: [dims.len]T =
# undefined;` filled by `inline for (table, 0..) |v, i| arr[i] = v;` and returned, that path
# does not exist: bench/bench_vec.zig buildPlan and buildSeedNames were four such errors.
# WHAT IT ADDS. A proof used only from lowerFor. Each level needs exactly one zero-based
# index-range input — a `.for_range` node; Ast.fullSlice does not cover it — whose capture is
# a plain `|x, i|` name, and every input's exact compile-time length > 0, all read through
# the EXISTING FileCache.fixedArrayLenOf and .comptimeIntValueOf. The body must be exactly ONE
# statement: the filling assignment, or a single nested `for`, recursed into; the LHS index
# chain must be exactly the enclosing counters, and each dimension exactly as long as the
# counter that walks it. Only then is one `.pointer_write` — the statement emitWritesInLhs
# already emits — appended to natural_exit, BEFORE any `else` is lowered onto it. It acts in
# transfer's `.pointer_write` arm in cfg_transfer, NOT in transferAssign: that comment in
# emitWritesInLhs named the wrong function and is corrected here, no behaviour moving. The
# counter query runs past the cheap gates only, and an open `0..` reuses the read length.
# WHAT IT REFUSES, each pinned by a test that must still report: a body that is not one
# statement or whose statement is neither an assignment nor a `for`; a value carrying
# `undefined`, `break`, `continue` or `return`; an `else` on a nested loop; a constant LHS
# index; a range not starting at 0 or whose length is not the dimension; a runtime-length or
# zero-length input; a nested loop filling part of a row, or an outer body filling part of the
# rows; and a payload token that is not one. That token is COMPUTED by fullForComponents —
# lastToken(last_input)+3, one more after a comma — so a payloadless `for (0..n)` sends it
# PAST the statement; it is now bounded and anchored on a `|` and a capture token before the
# scan. Unpinned on purpose: that loop binds nothing, so no valid LHS index equals its name.
# WHAT IT DOES NOT TOUCH. No CFG edge, no clear at `merge` in addition, and emitWritesInLhs
# with its rule that ANY indexed write clears the whole array's .undef is untouched: the
# certificate makes a whole-array clear honest, emitting one only when the write set equals
# the dimension set, and adds no element-granular state. No rule, severity, catalog entry or
# exclusion moves — all 113 stand, as do the reviewed intfromfloat_without_clamp warning and
# the dogfood self-check 0004 left failing. No name or input is special-cased; no benchmark,
# input file or exported API is touched.
# COVERAGE. 20 tests in src/flow/worklist.zig, named in that file: 4 expect no findings (1D
# fill, nested 2D fill, nested 3D with unequal dimensions, an `else` reading a filled buffer),
# 16 expect the rule SET to be exactly {use-undefined} and assert no count. Plus 2 helpers.
# EVIDENCE. Two runs of `zig test --test-filter "use_undefined:"`, 29 selected each, all 20 of
# these tests among them. The first, taken before the review correction was folded in here,
# passed in 7.4878057 s — waves/wave1-zbc-array-green-final.log. The second, over the bytes this
# file now carries, so with the payload bound, the moved query and the carried length present,
# passed in 13.7402239 s — waves/wave1-zbc-array-reviewed-green.log.
# BUILT AND GATED. The tree 0001-0005 produces was built with `zig build cli`, installed into a
# fresh prefix under an empty HOME with a REUSED work cache (276.1623 s, so not a cold install),
# and the full gate from that prefix exited 0 in 1061.0422 s: zbc selected=32 analyzed=32
# failed=0, 0 errors and the 3 reviewed intfromfloat advisories, so the four bench_vec
# use-undefined errors are gone from the project's own gate.
# NOT PROVED: no `zbc src/` self-run over this tree, so its self-finding count is unknown and
# the untouched default dogfood would still exit 1 on any finding; no three-run benchmark
# baseline, no remote GitHub Actions run, no vf engine run.
